          "order": 4,
          "explanation": "For all detail rows except status1=995, set status1 to newSts and add quantities from slots 2..10 whose statuses are below stsLimit.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "rs-batch-1809753850"
          ]
        },
        {
          "order": 5,
          "explanation": "Re-evaluate status1<>995 after the preceding UPDATE assigned newSts. For rows still matching, locate the first slot from 2..10 whose status reaches the limit and shift that slot and following suffix forward; zero unused tail slots and stamp the row. If the caller supplied newSts=995, this compaction UPDATE skips rows just assigned 995. This is a suffix-selection algorithm, not an independent filter of every later slot.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "rs-batch-1809753850"
          ]
        },
        {
          "order": 6,
          "explanation": "Set all shipment container statuses to newSts. For the independently supplied load ID, set leading status to newSts and trailing status to MIN of linked shipment trailing statuses; clear both failed flags and write local status dates/UTC stamp.",
